  "altyazi_taslagi": "Architecture-by-initialization design as a card cabinet. On CIFAR-10 the drawer rows ViT-Tiny and ResNet-18 cross the columns scratch (random init.) and ImageNet init.; each drawer gives its clean stage (epochs, learning rate) and seeds, one index card per run. The R32 bridge drawer keeps its own recipe; the sign on top is the AT recipe of the four cells.",
